    <article id="en-content">
      <p>Hi!</p>
      <p>I'm a software engineer with 20+ years of <a href="/resume/" title="Resume">professional experience</a>, currently focused
        on <a href="https://elixir-lang.org" title="link to Elixir website" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Elixir</a> and AI, but I've worked a lot with <a
          href="https://kotlinlang.org" title="link to Kotlin website" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kotlin</a>, <a href="https://java.com"
          title="link to Java website" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Java</a>, and <a
          href="https://www.ecma-international.org/publications-and-standards/standards/ecma-262"
          title="link to JavaScript specification" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">JavaScript</a> previously.</p>
      <p>All my professional experience is grounded in my undergraduate degree, completed in 2001 at the former UniverCidade,
        and in my postgraduate degrees in <em>&ldquo;Systems Analysis, Design and Management&rdquo;</em> and <em>&ldquo;Ergonomics,
          Usability and Human-Computer Interaction: Ergodesign and Interface Evaluation&rdquo;</em> at <a href="https://www.puc-rio.br" title="link to PUC-Rio website"
          target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PUC-Rio</a>.</p>
      <p>One of the best parts of my profession is continually specializing and seeking ways to improve and break down
        challenges in various areas of human knowledge, which means I'm always in a process of reconstruction.
      </p>
      <p>When I'm not working, you can find me taking care of my family, <a
          href="https://strava.com/athletes/raulpe7eira" title="link to Strava profile" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cycling</a>, <a
          href="https://imdb.com/user/ur28106453" title="link to IMDb profile" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">watching a movie</a>, <a
          href="https://last.fm/user/raulpereira" title="link to last.fm profile" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">listening to rock</a>
        or podcast, reading a comic book or a book, be it technology or just a children's book for my little ones.</p>
      <p>I also <a href="https://github.com/raulpe7eira" title="link to GitHub profile" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">push code</a>
        quite often, and <a href="https://instagram.com/raulpe7eira" title="link to Instagram profile"
          target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">show off pictures</a> from time to time.</p>
    </article>
